to that that there  is a big International movement going on  in the global economy right now I think  the IMF overnight have pointed to the  fact that  um other major European economies are  likely to go into recession Bloomberg I  think have said that it's very likely  that the us is going to go into  recession so when you when you put those  two things together a mistake in that  she sought to go too far too fast within  the setting of a global economic  situation of course this was forced upon  her and it took an enormous amount of  courage and Leadership to recognize that  make the change quickly apologize to the  British people which I think you would  reflect I hope is a contrast to a year  ago when the previous Prime Ministers  woes began she has fronted up to her  mistake very quickly  um and you know there are people in the  Parliamentary party who don't want that  to be an end of it but I think for an  awful lot of us we recognize that this  is a moment when the country needs its  government to knuckle down and get back  on with the day job  with all due respect Mr hippy she's  changed her mind because the markets  were tanking if the bank of England  hadn't stepped in the pensioners would  not have had their Pension funds  protected by the bank of England she had  no other choice than to do a vault fast  did you support when you heard the mini  Budget on the 23rd of September did you  think that's a good idea or did you  think what on Earth are they playing at  no I Look to be completely honest with  UK when the mini budget was presented to  us in the cabinet meeting uh immediately  for the before the Chancellor's  statement each and every one of those  measures was consistent with the  approach to growth that the government  was seeking and we all in gov in cabinet  accept Collective responsibility for the  fact that that mini budget was given and  it is important for all of us to be very  honest about that it's not just the  Prime Minister who made that mistake  although she has owned it and apologized  for it  are you sorry yes 100 I I just you know  the the reality is that that scale of  intervention  based on borrowing  at a moment when the guilts market was  as vulnerable as it is because of these  ldi mechanisms that have become so  pervasive uh within Pension funds  is not sustainable it was a it was a  mistake and the intervention that was  required from the bank of England  thereafter was very necessary but so too  has been the government's decision to  roll back on many of those measures  though it's important to note that the  national and insurance cut the stamp  Duty cut and crucially the intervention  on energy bills still stands but beyond  that the government has rode back  because it recognizes that the markets  are important the rate at which the  government borrows is absolutely  essential to the stability of our  economy and our spending plans going  forward and the Prime Minister has  addressed that  okay so the whole cabinet all supported  this mini budget before it was put to  the House of Commons is that what you  just said yes  okay so none of you knew what you were  doing so why on Earth are you still  running the country  well okay I'm not sure that I think that  that is fair comments I think that the  uh the budget was presented to cabinet  and each and every one of the measures  within it were in and off themselves  coherent with a plan to drive growth but  if you're asking why I think I as a  defense minister deserve to continue to  sit around the cabinet table or I would  reflect that we here in the ministry of  Defense are doing a good job of keeping  our nation safe at a time of incredible  Global insecurity my boss Ben Wallace is  in Washington this morning uh having the  sort of conversations that foreign  beyond belief really the fact that we're  at a time when these sort of  conversations are necessary  um I think that in this department we've  done a good job and we've got a good  record on which to stand and actually I  could say the same for every other  colleague around governments in their  Department too  to keep our country safe we need to keep  our economy safe and we saw immediately  that the markets thought you'd all lost  your minds  well I I think we're in violence  agreements I've been very honest with  you throughout this interview as the  Prime Minister was in her interview last  night that the reaction of the markets  caused a change in plan that was a plan  that was changed quickly and the prime  minister's owned and apologized for  but the fact is that the markets have  since been reassured and that is also a  good thing and a reflection of her  leadership and the fact that she now has  a Chancellor in number 11 in whom the  city has confidence and that is that is  a good thing  how many more mistakes can she afford to  make  well I suspect given how uh skittish our  politics are at the moment not very many  but she wouldn't have wanted to have  made the mistake that she's made  to her credit she has owned it and  apologized for it but my experience of  the Prime Minister when she was foreign  secretary and Secretary State for  international trade and the the  international facing departments work  quite closely as we deliver our nation's  foreign policy is that the Prime  Minister makes good decisions based on  the evidence she listens to her  officials and throughout her time as  Secretary of State for international  trade and foreign secretary I think a  record shows that there is no hiding  from the fact that a mistake was made  around the mini budget but it's one that  she has owned and apologized for and now  crucially the country needs its  government to get on with the task at  hand because there is an awful lot in  the entry  how many more mistakes can she make for  you  well I I just so many hey I just said I  I don't think that there's the  opportunity to make any more mistakes  because the nation needs a government  that is governing well and is making  good decisions the nation also needs a  government that is honest where mistakes  are made  okay and if she does make any more  mistakes from what you're saying she's  toast  um it does look as though potentially  your department may have to suffer Cuts  uh we're hearing that potentially 15  percent across the board is what the uh  foreign the previous foreign secretary  now uh Chancellor de facto prime  minister some people are calling him if  there are cuts to your department that  mean that we don't see the two and a  half percent uh of GDP spent on defense  three percent by 2028 what does that  mean for you  well there's there's a number of things  that you said there that weren't quite  right if you'll allow so the commitment  that the Prime Minister made is three  percent by 2030 uh and to be clear  um like the Secretary of State  um that is something that I believe must  be delivered given the need to keep our  nation safe in increasingly uncertain  times you you cannot have Prosperity at  home or internationally without security  and that is a really good reason to be  investing in defense now if in the very  immediate term there is a requirement to  look at what we can do to help the  treasury out that's a discussion for the  chancellor to have with the secretary of  state but I am confident that the Prime  Minister and the chancellor and the  foreign secretary and frankly everyone  else around government understands the  importance of investing in our nation's  armed forces and our defenses at a time  when the UK interest at home and abroad  is under such threat okay so if I said  to you if there were Cuts in the  ministry defense budget in the short  term would that impact on our support  for Ukraine I know what you would say  you would say no so I would then have to  put it to you if I may Mr hupy that  would mean Brits uh elsewhere around the  world would find themselves in a  difficult position  well okay I think that that is true  there is there are some very hard  choices to make and we have to be very  clear on why we are doing what we're  doing in Ukraine why it's so important  to be supporting the Ukrainian Armed  Forces why it's so important to be  investing in our own Defense Forces at  the moment and that's because the cost  of not doing those things is that we  will be living in a Europe in a world  whereby it has been shown that if you  are willing to be belligerent and use  Force to threaten the sovereignty of  another country you can succeed but the  International Community loses patience  that it blinks and it dips in and you  get your way and what that does is set  us on a trajectory for the rest of this  Century whereby we will be having to  spend a lot more on our defense and  security and where our economy will be  profoundly impacted by that insecurity  so this is this is about investing now  in the ukrainians so that they can do do  the right thing in order to draw a line  underneath Putin's aggression to show  that a rules-based International System  still applies in this century  and I think that all of your viewers  would agree but that is the right thing  to be doing because the alternative is a  world that is more unstable more  insecure and a whole lot less prosperous  Mr hippie Authority if you would please  sir about our Top Guns heading off to  China to train potentially future  enemies how to fly planes  yeah and it's been a concern within the  mod for a number of years uh  counter-intelligence people have been  looking at it closely uh we are we have  approached the people that are involved  uh and been clear with them that it is  our expectation that they would not  continue to be part of that organization  and we are going to put into law that  once people have been given that warning  it would become an offense to then go uh  forward and continue with that training  um China is a competitor that  um is threatening the UK interest uh in  many places around the world it's also  an important trading partner but there  is no secret in their attempt to gain  access to our secrets and the  recruitment of our Pilots uh in order to  understand the capabilities of our air  force is clearly a concern to us and the  intelligence uh part of the mad  okay so don't be a tray to come home  before you can't and we put you in jail  well I yeah don't go and train foreign  Air Forces without checking with the mod  whether they're a foreign Air Force that  we want to see you train would be a  pretty good rule  okay good to see you Mr hoopy thank you  very much indeed for joining us

